+		 * Zone sizes deliberately match the vendor firmware's own ramoops
+		 * node, so the console zone lands at the same physical address and
+		 * length in both kernels. That makes a failed boot here readable
+		 * from the stock kernel's /sys/fs/pstore afterwards, which is the
+		 * only post-mortem channel this board has: the debug UART is not
+		 * accessible on a retail unit. pstore allocates dmesg, console then
+		 * pmsg in that order, so any extra dmesg record zone would shift
+		 * the console zone and break that compatibility.
