+ * (abl-final-fdt.dts:13288). Nothing describes its voltage: the vendor tree
+ * carries a bare GPIO with no rail behind it, and the bridge chip's supply is
+ * generated on the folio side. startup-delay-us preserves the vendor's 2 ms
+ * rail-to-reset delay.
+ *
+ * Keep the provider under the real simple-bus. ABL applies the vendor dtbo
+ * after the boot image DTB and has already been observed rewriting or dropping
+ * root-level additions, while children of /soc@0 survive in the live FDT.
